  "text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n2026 Satellite Location Press Release - News - Elections - Woodbury County, Iowa\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n Skip to content\n \n\n \n\n \n Woodbury County\n Iowa • Elections\n \n \n\n \n\n Facebook Contact Us\n \n \n\n \n \nVote \n \n \nRegister to Vote\n \nAbsentee Voting\n \nMaps\n \nMilitary/Overseas Voting\n \nPrecincts\n \nVoter ID\n \n \n \nElections \n \n \nUpcoming Elections\n \nPast Elections\n \nSample Ballots\n \nPrecinct Election Officials\n \nTypes of Elections\n \n \n \nElected Officials \n \n \nFederal\n \nState\n \nCounty\n \nCity\n \nSchool Board\n \nTownship\n \nDrainage\n \n \n \nCandidates\n \nNews\n \nFAQ\n \n \n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n Woodbury County\nElections\n\n\n\n Due to staffing and security needs, the ballot drop box is no longer in use. Voted ballots can be returned by mail or in person to 620 Douglas St, Rm 103. Other Election News & Satellite Locations \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nNews\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n2026 Satellite Location Press Release\n \n September 22, 2026 \nWOODBURY COUNTY, Iowa — The Woodbury County Election Office has announced satellite voting locations and key deadlines for the upcoming General Election on Tuesday, November 3, 2026. \n \n\nWoodbury County voters can cast an early in-person ballot at a satellite voting site or at the Woodbury County Auditor’s Office, or vote at their assigned polling place on Election Day. \n \n\nSatellite Voting Locations & Schedules \n \n\n1. Long Lines Family Center \n \n\n401 Gordon Drive, Sioux City, IA (East Entrance) \n \n \n \nBallots Available: All Woodbury County ballot styles \n \nWeekdays: October 14 – November 2 | 8:00 AM – 4:30 PM \n \nSaturday Hours: October 17, October 24, & October 31 | 9:00 AM – 3:00 PM \n \n \n\n2. Briar Cliff University \n \n\n3303 Rebecca Street, Sioux City, IA (St. Francis Center – Gantz Boardroom) \n \n \n \nBallots Available: All Woodbury County ballot styles \n \nDate & Hours: Monday, October 19 | 9:00 AM – 3:00 PM \n \n \n\n3. Western Iowa Tech Community College \n \n\n4647 Stone Avenue, Sioux City, IA (Robert Kiser Building – Entrance 1 or 3) \n \n \n \nBallots Available: All Woodbury County ballot styles \n \nDates & Hours: Tuesday, October 20 & Wednesday, October 21 | 9:00 AM – 3:00 PM \n \n \n\n4. Morningside University \n \n\n3609 Peters Avenue, Sioux City, IA (Olsen Student Center – Yockey Family Room) \n \n \n \nBallots Available: All Woodbury County ballot styles \n \nDate & Hours: Thursday, October 22 | 9:00 AM – 3:00 PM \n \n \n\n5. Shepherd of Peace Church \n \n\n203 Port Neal Road, Sergeant Bluff, IA \n \n \n \nBallots Available: Sergeant Bluff School District ballot styles ONLY \n \nDate & Hours: Monday, October 26 | 2:00 PM – 8:00 PM \n \n \n\nIn-Person Early Voting at the Auditor’s Office \n \n\nVoters may also cast early ballots at the Woodbury County Courthouse Auditor’s Office (620 Douglas St, Rm 103, Sioux City, IA): \n \n \n \nWeekdays: October 14 – November 2 | 8:00 AM – 4:30 PM \n \nSpecial Friday Hours: October 30th | 8:00 AM – 5:00 PM \n \nSpecial Saturday Hours: October 31 | 8:00 AM – 5:00 PM \n \n \n\nImportant Election Deadlines & Reminders \n \n \n \nOctober 19, 2026: \n \n \n \nPre-Registration Deadline: Last day to pre-register to vote. \n \nAbsentee Request Deadline: Last day to submit an absentee ballot request form to receive a ballot by mail. \n \n \n \nNovember 3, 2026 (Election Day): \n \n \nPolling Hours: 7:00 AM – 8:00 PM at assigned precinct locations. Find your location at elections.woodburycountyiowa.gov/search. \n \nAbsentee Ballot Return Deadline: Mailed or hand-delivered absentee ballots must be received at the Auditor’s Office by 8:00 PM on Election Day. \n \n \n \nImportant Policy Note: The ballot drop box is no longer in use. Ballots must be returned via mail or delivered directly to the Auditor’s Office. \n \nSame-Day Registration: Available at all satellite locations, the Auditor’s Office, and Election Day polling places for voters needing to register or update their information after October 19. \n \n \n\nFor More Information \n \n\nFor questions regarding voting locations, voter registration, or absentee voting, contact the Woodbury County Elections Department at (712) 279-6465 or visit elections.woodburycountyiowa.gov. \n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n \nMore News\n \n\n \n2026 Public Measure 1: Constitutional Amendment - Full Language\n \n October 12, 2026 Ballots will show the Summary of the Statewide Constitutional Amendment. Review full language here. \n\n \n \n\n\n\n\nThis webpage was printed on October 17, 2026. For the most current election-related information, visit the Woodbury County, Iowa, Elections website at https://elections.woodburycountyiowa.gov.\n\n\n\n \n\n Woodbury County Courthouse\n\n 620 Douglas St. - Room 103\n \nSioux City, IA 51101\n\n Contact Us\n\n Accessibility\n\n Woodbury County Website\n \n \nOffice Hours\n\n Monday - Friday\n \n8AM - 4:30PM \n \nContact Information\n\n Phone: (712) 279-6465\n \nFax: (712) 2796629 \n \n\n \n\n Facebook Contact Us\n \n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n \npowered by \n\n\n\n\n\n"
}
